  "label": "ITIN-filing gate firing case — §6013(h) electing spouse (manual case)",
  "story": "Manual regression case for task #47's own follow-up stretch goal (§6013(h) spouse-ITIN gate): a single primary filer WITH a valid SSN on file (isolating this from us_itin_gate_required.json's primary-only case) who elects §6013(h) joint treatment with a spouse who has no SSN/ITIN/ATIN on file, and no Form W-7 application recorded as filed. Fires itin_application_required (severity: critical, spouse-only wording) and the form_w7 document trigger, purely off the spouse's missing ID — the primary taxpayer's own ssn_or_itin_type is 'ssn', so this exercises a branch us_itin_gate_required.json's own primary-missing case cannot reach. No golden fixture or fuzz-corpus profile ever sets s6013h_joint_election true with spouse_ssn_or_itin_type left at 'none' (the field didn't exist before this task), so nothing else in either regression suite reaches this path.",
